  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set needed to trace the FastAPI \u2194 httpx contract-drift investigation:\n\n**FastAPI request validation chain**\n- `fastapi/routing.py` \u2014 `get_request_handler`, content-type negotiation (`content_type_value`), and where `request.json()`/`request.form()` is dispatched before dependency solving\n- `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` \u2014 `solve_dependencies`, `request_body_to_args`, `get_body_field` (the core body\u2192param binding logic, embed rules, None/default handling)\n- `fastapi/_compat.py` \u2014 Pydantic v1/v2 compatibility shims: `ModelField.validate`, `field_annotation_is_complex`, union/sequence detection used to decide how nested models and unions are parsed\n- `fastapi/params.py` \u2014 `Body`, `Form`, `File` field-info classes (media_type, embed defaults)\n- `fastapi/exceptions.py` \u2014 `RequestValidationError` (surfaces as the 422)\n- `fastapi/encoders.py` \u2014 `jsonable_encoder`, relevant for round-tripping nested/union types\n- `fastapi/dependencies/models.py` \u2014 `Dependant` dataclass shape referenced throughout\n\n**httpx request encoding chain**\n- `httpx/_content.py` \u2014 `encode_request`/`encode_json`/`encode_urlencoded_data`/`encode_multipart_data`, the actual Content-Type + body-encoding logic\n- `httpx/_models.py` \u2014 `Request.__init__`/`_prepare` (header auto-population, Content-Length vs Transfer-Encoding)\n- `httpx/_client.py` \u2014 public `request()`/`post()` etc. surface that accepts `json=`/`data=`/`content=`\n- `httpx/_multipart.py`, `httpx/_utils.py` (`primitive_value_to_str`, None\u2192`\"\"` coercion), `httpx/_types.py`, `httpx/_api.py`\n\nThese cover both sides of the drift: FastAPI's Pydantic-v2 validation path (nested-model/union/default handling in `_compat.py` + `dependencies/utils.py`) against httpx's `json.dumps`-based encoding (`_content.py`) and its `primitive_value_to_str` None-handling in form/query encoding (`_utils.py`).",
